# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Exercise the explicit contract between internal communication and Newton.
#
# The Python driver invokes this file four times:
#   1. comm_off_newton_on;
#   2. comm_off_newton_off;
#   3. comm_on_newton_on; and
#   4. internal communication with Newton off, which must fail clearly.
# The successful runs use exactly the same static crystal. Their atom-ID-aligned
# energies and forces must agree within the tolerances in run_regression.py.

variable model index model.ptb
variable comm index off
variable newton_setting index on
variable prediction_dump index newton.lammpstrj
# These defaults make the file runnable by itself. run_regression.py overrides
# them with `-var` to create the three configurations described above.

units metal
atom_style atomic
boundary p p p
newton ${newton_setting}
processors 2 1 1
# MACE-MP medium-0b3 with the default head predicts a zero-pressure BCC Ti
# lattice constant of 3.2663 Angstrom. Start from that relaxed bulk cell before
# adding the deterministic distortion below.
lattice bcc 3.2663
region box block 0 4 0 4 0 4 units lattice
create_box 22 box
create_atoms 22 box
# A perfect bcc crystal has nearly zero forces by symmetry and would let some
# broken force-communication paths pass. Create a deterministic rough plane near
# the x-domain boundary (x=2 lattice units for this 2x1x1 decomposition). The
# displacement is deliberately large enough to be visually obvious in a dump
# viewer while remaining well below a nearest-neighbor distance.
region defect block 1.65 2.35 0 4 0 4 units lattice
group defect region defect
displace_atoms defect random 0.45 0.35 0.35 20260623 units box
# Masses are required during run setup but do not affect this static evaluation.
mass * 1.0

# `comm` and `newton` together select the specialized model variant. Padding is
# generous here because this test targets Newton behavior, not recompilation.
pair_style chemtrain cuda 0.85 comm ${comm} capacity/atom 2.0 capacity/edge 4.0
pair_coeff * * ${model}
neighbor 2.0 bin
neigh_modify every 1 delay 0 check no

thermo 1
thermo_style custom step atoms pe pxx pyy pzz pxy pxz pyz
thermo_modify format float %.16g
compute atom_energy all pe/atom
dump prediction all custom 1 ${prediction_dump} id type x y z fx fy fz c_atom_energy
dump_modify prediction sort id format float %.16g first yes

# `run 0` is an actual force/energy evaluation, but advances zero timesteps.
# LAMMPS builds the neighbor list, calls the pair style, prints thermo output,
# and writes the requested first dump frame. Static evaluation is intentional:
# changing coordinates would confound a direct Newton-on/Newton-off comparison.
run 0
